course: dictionary
lesson: 5314
title: Many meanings of keep
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word keep has more than one meaning, so you need the words around it to find the right one. «If Gran says "keep the change", the extra money stays with you.» Here keep means to go on having something and not give it away.
explain: «Any secret someone asks you to keep from your parents is a reason to tell them.» Secret is the clue. To keep a secret means not to tell it. Try the swap: if "not to tell" fits the sentence, you have found the right meaning.
explain: «In a fair test you change only one thing and keep everything else the same.» Here keep means stay the same. «Old diving bells kept people dry under water» works the same way: it means the bells made people stay dry. Read the whole sentence before you choose a meaning.
fact: Keep is a verb (keep, keeps, kept, keeping). It is also a noun in «your keep», which means food and a home.
fact: To keep something means to go on having it and not give it away.
fact: To keep doing something means to go on doing it, as in «keep on».
fact: «For keeps» means forever, and to keep a promise means not to break it.
fact: Food that keeps stays good to eat.
exercise: «If Gran says "keep the change", what does keep mean?» | To count the money again | *To go on having it and not give it back | To give the money away
exercise: In «keep a secret», what does keep mean? | To write it down in a book | *To not tell it or break it | To shout it out loud
exercise: «Food that keeps stays good to eat.» What does keeps mean here? | To get cold and hard | *To stay good to eat | To run away from the kitchen
test: «Old diving bells kept people dry under water.» What does kept mean here? | Dried them with a towel | Made them wet | *Made them stay dry
test: What does «for keeps» mean? | Only on Sundays | *Forever | For a short while
exam: Which formal word could replace keep in «keep everything else the same»? | Dance | Lose | *Maintain | Shout
